WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:01.410
- [Instructor] We are asked, what could

00:01.410 --> 00:02.990
be the equation of p?

00:02.990 --> 00:06.120
And we have graph of our
polynomial p right over here,

00:06.120 --> 00:07.365
you could view this as the graph

00:07.365 --> 00:10.860
of y is equal to p of x.

00:10.860 --> 00:14.310
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:14.310 --> 00:16.000
All right, now let's
work on this together,

00:16.000 --> 00:18.245
and you can see that all
the choices have p of x,

00:18.245 --> 00:19.943
in factored form where it's very easy

00:19.943 --> 00:22.468
to identify the zeros or the x values

00:22.468 --> 00:25.280
that would make our
polynomial equal to zero.

00:25.280 --> 00:26.760
And we could also look at this graph

00:26.760 --> 00:29.180
and we can see what the zeros are.

00:29.180 --> 00:31.534
This is where we're going
to intersect the x-axis,

00:31.534 --> 00:33.910
also known as the x-intercepts.

00:33.910 --> 00:37.630
So you can see when x is
equal to negative four,

00:37.630 --> 00:42.630
we have a zero because our
polynomial is zero there.

00:42.820 --> 00:46.040
So we know p of negative
four is equal to zero.

00:46.040 --> 00:49.210
We also know that p of, looks like 1 1/2,

00:49.210 --> 00:50.300
or I could say 3/2.

00:50.300 --> 00:53.480
p of 3/2 is equal to zero,

00:53.480 --> 00:57.478
and we also know that p
of three is equal to zero.

00:57.478 --> 01:00.970
So let's look for an
expression where that is true.

01:00.970 --> 01:02.328
And because it's in factored form,

01:02.328 --> 01:05.879
each of the parts of the product

01:05.879 --> 01:08.235
will probably make our polynomial zero

01:08.235 --> 01:10.520
for one of these zeroes.

01:10.520 --> 01:12.632
So let's see if, if in
order for our polynomial

01:12.632 --> 01:15.760
to be equal to zero when x
is equal to negative four,

01:15.760 --> 01:16.814
we probably want to have a term

01:16.814 --> 01:19.810
that has an x plus four in it.

01:19.810 --> 01:21.380
Or we want to have a, I should say,

01:21.380 --> 01:24.160
a product that has an x plus four in it.

01:24.160 --> 01:25.152
Because x plus four is equal

01:25.152 --> 01:28.198
to zero when x is equal to negative four.

01:28.198 --> 01:29.902
Well we have an x plus four there,

01:29.902 --> 01:32.010
and we have an x plus four there.

01:32.010 --> 01:34.720
So I'm liking choices B and D so far.

01:34.720 --> 01:39.720
Now for this second root, we have p of 3/2

01:39.880 --> 01:41.194
is equal to zero so I would look

01:41.194 --> 01:46.194
for something like x
minus 3/2 in our product.

01:46.980 --> 01:49.590
I don't see an x minus 3/2 here,

01:49.590 --> 01:51.070
but as we've mentioned in other videos

01:51.070 --> 01:53.580
you can also multiply
these times constants.

01:53.580 --> 01:54.413
So if I were to multiply,

01:54.413 --> 01:56.490
let's see to get rid
of this fraction here,

01:56.490 --> 01:59.270
if I multiply by two this
would be the same thing as,

01:59.270 --> 02:01.060
let me scroll down a little bit,

02:01.060 --> 02:04.320
same thing as two x minus three.

02:04.320 --> 02:05.470
And you could test that out,

02:05.470 --> 02:08.393
two x minus three is equal to
zero when x is equal to 3/2.

02:09.280 --> 02:14.040
And let's see, we have a two x
minus three right over there.

02:14.040 --> 02:15.793
So choice D is looking awfully good,

02:15.793 --> 02:18.097
but let's just verify
it with this last one.

02:18.097 --> 02:20.720
For p of three to be equal to zero,

02:20.720 --> 02:22.204
we could have an expression

02:22.204 --> 02:25.260
like x minus three in the product

02:25.260 --> 02:27.880
because this is equal to zero
when x is equal to three,

02:27.880 --> 02:30.550
and we indeed have that right over there.

02:30.550 --> 02:34.440
So choice D is looking very good.

02:34.440 --> 02:36.225
When x is equal to negative four,

02:36.225 --> 02:39.559
this part of our product is equal

02:39.559 --> 02:43.010
to zero which makes the
whole thing equal to zero.

02:43.010 --> 02:47.660
When x is equal to 3/2,
two x minus three is equal

02:47.660 --> 02:50.110
to zero which makes the
entire product equal to zero.

02:50.110 --> 02:52.910
And when x minus, and when
an x is equal to three,

02:52.910 --> 02:54.990
it makes x minus three equal to zero.

02:54.990 --> 02:56.473
Zero times something, times something

02:56.473 --> 02:58.913
is going to be equal to zero.
